From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:14:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: gemini-lid: light the backlight on open only if it was
 lit

The policy turns the backlight off when the lid closes and on when it
opens, whatever the display was doing. On the Gemini the display had
been blanked before a lid-close suspend. After the lid opened, the
panel stayed dark with the backlight lit, and the battery current read
about 134 mA higher than before the suspend.

Record at the close whether the backlight was lit, and on the open turn
it back on only then. A display blanked before the close stays dark,
and its own unblank, by DPMS or the console, restores the backlight as
usual.
---
 drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
index 873eae73d..00fbf68b2 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
@@ -25,6 +25,8 @@ static DEFINE_MUTEX(lid_lock);
 static struct input_dev *lid_keyboard;
 static bool lid_exiting;
 static bool lid_applied_closed;
+/* The backlight was lit when the lid closed, so the open lights it again. */
+static bool lid_backlight_was_on;
 
 static void gemini_lid_apply(bool closed)
 {
@@ -47,10 +49,17 @@ static void gemini_lid_apply(bool closed)
 	if (bd) {
 		mutex_lock(&bd->ops_lock);
 		if (bd->ops) {
-			if (closed)
+			/*
+			 * Restore only what the close turned off: a display
+			 * blanked before the close, by DPMS or a console blank,
+			 * stays dark, with no backlight behind a sleeping panel.
+			 */
+			if (closed) {
+				lid_backlight_was_on = !backlight_is_blank(bd);
 				backlight_disable(bd);
-			else
+			} else if (lid_backlight_was_on) {
 				backlight_enable(bd);
+			}
 		}
 		mutex_unlock(&bd->ops_lock);
 	}
